<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The monochrome layer, for Android's themed icons.

    Worth having rather than omitting, and the reason is no longer stylistic.
    Android 16 QPR2 auto-themes any app that does not ship this layer, applying a
    colour filter to the existing icon; the Play Developer Distribution Agreement
    reserves the right to recolour app icons too. Shipping a deliberate silhouette
    means a themed-icon user sees something designed. Omitting it means they see
    whatever the platform decided your icon looked like.

    The system tints this layer and preserves alpha, so only the shape survives.
    It is therefore the same geometry as the foreground, counters and all: a
    themed icon that differed in silhouette from the real one would be a different
    mark wearing the same name.
-->
